 substituting $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =3.463$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.463\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266049 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266050 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266051 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266052 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266053 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1041 "selection" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266053 13194139533921 true] [17592186266048 1110 #uuid "45ce2e21-bef8-5bb3-9b61-46e5fc5afa8b" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266049 1034 "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.463\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266049 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533921 true] [17592186266049 1111 #uuid "099f0768-b014-55cb-b63b-f7d85b833073" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266050 1034 "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.281\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266050 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533921 true] [17592186266050 1111 #uuid "7d180bc9-48d4-52b0-a142-7e634cdda919" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266051 1034 "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.974\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266051 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533921 true] [17592186266051 1111 #uuid "1beab5ef-a033-5ba1-a636-839356156fd8" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266052 1034 "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.281\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533921 true] [17592186266052 1111 #uuid "5a62b093-64a7-58f2-8818-0e03ab067f8b" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266053 1034 "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.463\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266053 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533921 true] [17592186266053 1111 #uuid "9644d12d-871f-59c2-8a4b-3ddc88f4b08c" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266054 1017 #edb/ref 17592186266055 13194139533921 true] [17592186266054 1089 "q-107427" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266054 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533921 true] [17592186266054 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953226/assets/7b72c7db59c20e5b3a86cde6b212cfdd88204588d0e5cca29524ba485aee5346.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." 13194139533921 true] [17592186266054 1113 #uuid "fd5f7e02-06fb-58a5-8972-0a228aeaf734" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266054 1145 "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the first quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\n$$" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266056 13194139533921 true] [17592186266055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266057 13194139533921 true] [17592186266055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266058 13194139533921 true] [17592186266055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266059 13194139533921 true] [17592186266055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266060 13194139533921 true] [17592186266055 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533921 true] [17592186266055 1041 "selection" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266055 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266060 13194139533921 tru