shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533921 true] [17592186266110 1113 #uuid "786f2ec5-3904-5211-975b-9f7327fe00cc" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266110 1145 "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-2+3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{3}{2})| \\\\  & ≈2.159.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\theta =2.159$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.159\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266112 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266113 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266114 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266115 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266116 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1041 "selection" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266116 13194139533921 true] [17592186266111 1110 #uuid "d7a958f8-baab-5993-91b6-96ce675043fa" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266112 1034 "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.859\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533921 true] [17592186266112 1111 #uuid "178963aa-5fc4-5b26-a28c-3f4b2abddcc7" 13194139533921 true] [17592186266113 1034 "z=\\s